  "root_problem": "Dispute tickets abruptly doubled from a stable ~600/month baseline (Jun-Jul 2026) to ~1180-1260/month in Aug-Sep 2026 (E-03), and the best-supported mechanism is that a billing import validation rule change around August is producing incorrect bills in the billing-import step of meter-to-cash for both actual-read and estimated-read accounts (H-RULE-CHANGE-DEFECT). This is evidenced by disputed bills skewing 59% toward ACTUAL reads rather than estimates (E-04), which rules out field-read-shortfall and AMI-delivery estimate-substitution mechanisms as dominant drivers, while CS response times remaining within SLA (E-02) rules out a CS-side process cause."
